            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery bypass surgery for patients with left main coronary lesions due to Takayasu's arteritis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>661-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two patients with documented Takayasu's arteritis and severe left main coronary lesion were operated on. The first patient was a 17-year-old boy operated with a double saphenous vein coronary artery bypass graft in 1982, the patient survived 12 years but died suddenly due to associated aortic insufficiency. The second case was a 46-year-old female patient who was successfully operated on.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
